      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the EPD_Driver sheet, C1 is drawn with value 0.1 µF / 16 V, hanging off the Display_Power_Switch node to GND.",
      "expected": "The specification's PDI-reference matching table states that Meshinger's C1 belongs to the '1 µF/25 V' group (the row 'C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V'), i.e. C1 should be 1 µF with a 25 V rating, consistent with the G1-group charge-pump/boost capacitance.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EPD_Driver.kicad_sch (page 3/4): 'C1 0.1uF/16V' between Display_Power_Switch and GND"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default"}
      ],
      "impact": "The boost/charge-pump capacitance feeding the e-paper panel is reduced tenfold and its voltage rating dropped from 25 V to 16 V. The EPD multiplier may fail to develop the required VGH/VGL swing reliably (poor or incomplete refresh), and the 16 V dielectric is marginal for a node that sees boosted panel voltages, risking capacitor breakdown.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build matches the specification almost exactly (SKW92A, FAN53610 rail, BBQ10KBD, NTR2101P display switch, PDI EPD boost parts, barrel-jack battery-disconnect, HW_RESET switch, unconnected-in-netlist Ethernet noted as an open item). The one deviation is C1 on the EPD_Driver sheet, drawn as 0.1 µF/16 V where the intended design specifies 1 µF/25 V, which would degrade the e-paper boost/charge-pump performance and reduce its voltage headroom."
}

